## Why This Is Asked

This question introduces an E2E test around a common SaaS workflow (onboarding) plus a deterministic file export. It stresses flaky networks and idempotent exports, which are frequent real-world issues.

## Key Concepts

- E2E testing with UI and API mocks
- File download validation
- Autosave and state persistence
- Retry/duplicate prevention

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example Playwright snippet
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';

test('onboarding + export produces single CSV', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.goto('/login');
  await page.fill('#email','test@example.com');
  await page.fill('#pass','secret');
  await page.click('#login');

  // Step 1
  await page.fill('#name','ACME');
  await page.click('#next');

  // Step 2
  await page.fill('#company','ACME Corp');
  await page.click('#finish');

  // Mock export and latency
  await page.route('**/export/csv', route => {
    route.fulfill({ status: 200, body: 'id,name\n1,A' });
  });

  // Trigger export and verify single file
  await page.click('#export');
  const [ download ] = await Promise.all([
    page.waitForEvent('download'),
    page.click('#confirm-export')
  ]);
  const path = await download.path();
  expect(path).not.toBeNull();
});
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you scale this to multiple report types?
- How would you test export failures and retry backoffs?

## Why This Is Asked
This question validates the candidate's ability to design comprehensive end-to-end tests for complex ML-in-the-loop systems. It tests understanding of multi-tenant isolation, data seeding strategies, ML model drift handling, real-time collaboration under load, and audit integrity.

## Key Concepts
- End-to-end testing of AI-assisted labeling workflows
- Multi-tenant data isolation and access control verification
- Model drift injection, detection, and graceful degradation
- Audit log integrity, sequencing, and tamper-evidence
- Concurrency control and conflict resolution in collaborative labeling

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo e2e test outline for AI labeling workflow
describe('AI labeling E2E', () => {
  it('handles full labeling lifecycle with ML suggestions', async () => {
    // Seed tenant data
    const project = await createProject({ tenantId: 'tenant-1' });
    await seedLabelingData(project.id, SAMPLE_DATASET);

    // Inject model drift
    await simulateModelDrift({ driftType: 'concept', severity: 'high' });

    // Create and process labeling task
    const task = await createLabelingTask(project.id);
    const suggestions = await getMLSuggestions(task.id);

    // Annotator workflow
    const annotation = await approveSuggestion(task.id, suggestions[0].id);
    expect(annotation.status).toBe('approved');

    // Verify audit integrity
    const auditLog = await getAuditLog(task.id);
    expect(auditLog).toBeSequenced();
  });

  it('handles 200 concurrent annotators', async () => {
    const annotators = await createAnnotators(200);
    const results = await Promise.all(
      annotators.map(a => a.submitAnnotation())
    );
    expect(results.conflictRate).toBeLessThan(0.01);
  });
});
```

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses practical E2E skills: gating UX with feature flags, deterministic tests, data seeding, and test isolation using Cypress or Playwright.

## Key Concepts

- Feature flags and gating
- Test data seeding per run
- LocalStorage state as idempotence marker
- Network/mocks to deterministically simulate flag responses
- Time-bounded execution for beginner scenarios

## Code Example

```javascript
// Playwright skeleton
test('onboarding respects flag', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.route('**/flags**', r => r.fulfill({ status: 200, body: JSON.stringify({ onboarding: true }) }));
  await page.goto('https://app.local/');
  await expect(page.locator('#onboard-modal')).toBeVisible();
  await page.locator('#finish').click();
  const stored = await page.evaluate(() => localStorage.getItem('onboarding_complete'));
  expect(stored).toBe('true');
  await page.reload();
  await expect(page.locator('#onboard-modal')).toBeHidden();
});
```

